o chemotherapy in some first-line metastatic cervical cancer regimens, acting by inhibiting growth of new blood vessels that supply tumors. [Data: Entities (4245, 2274, 491); Relationships (8845, 3961)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Adverse effects and long-term risks are prominent, including hypersensitivity, neurologic effects, fertility impacts, and pregnancy cautions\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The data enumerates multiple adverse effects associated with chemotherapy broadly, including tingling or numbness and rash, and emphasizes that chemotherapy can damage normal healthy cells throughout the whole body. This frames side effects as a systemic consequence of mechanism (targeting rapidly dividing cells). [Data: Entities (5983, 5984, 6161, 5999, 4272); Relationships (13655, 13656, 14098, 13658, 8935)]\\n\\nSpecific high-salience risks include hypersensitivity reactions that can be life-threatening with repeat carboplatin exposure, and cisplatin-associated tinnitus. Long-term risks are also explicitly noted, including development of other cancers years later and infertility (inability to have children). [Data: Entities (2338, 676, 4835, 5095, 5096); Relationships (4097, 10479, 11188, 11190)]\\n\\nPregnancy-related caution is directly represented: treatments can cause birth defects, and the data advises avoiding pregnancy/impregnation during chemotherapy. [Data: Entities (4293); Relationships (8997)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Clinical staging/biomarker-linked chemotherapy recommendations appear, but only at a high level in this dataset\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Chemotherapy is linked to ovarian cancer staging via a relationship stating that for newly diagnosed stage 2, 3, and 4 ovarian cancers, chemotherapy is recommended after surgery. This is represented as a general recommendation rather than a detailed protocol in the provided graph. [Data: Entities (2290, 491); Relationships (3943)]\\n\\nThe dataset also includes stage-2 substaging no